Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.53,0:00:15.05,Show_Title,Screen,0000,0000,0000,,{\fad(0,825)\pos(320,10)\3c&H8ECEDD&}JUJUTSU KAISEN\N{\fs16\bord0\fscy100\c&HDEDCE0&}Shibuya Incident
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.48,0:01:46.01,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,Do you remember
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.57,0:01:50.71,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,the ways to rid cursed \Nspirits from our world?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.62,0:01:56.20,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,Regardless of which method is pursued,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.20,0:02:00.12,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,it means advancing humanity \Nto the next stage.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.42,0:02:05.76,Italics,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,Now, I need to buy time for Larue to act.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.59,0:02:09.93,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,Humanity's next stage is
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.93,0:02:13.15,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,freeing itself from cursed energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.09,0:02:18.12,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,No. It's optimizing cursed energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.50,0:02:26.41,Main,Yuji,0000,0000,0000,,Uh, I don't get it, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.80,0:02:32.92,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,I thought you already gave on your plan \Ntwelve years ago, when Zen'in Toji died.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.92,0:02:35.92,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,I was talking to Geto-kun, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.97,0:02:38.67,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,Well, whatever.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.51,0:02:41.66,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,I went back to my original idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.66,0:02:45.29,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,Besides, there's a big hole \Nin your optimization plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.68,0:02:51.31,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,Extremely few sorcerers and cursed spirits \Nemerge in other countries compared to Japan.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.19,0:02:57.43,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,So Tengen's barriers should be \Nindispensable to your optimization plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.50,0:03:02.47,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,Using Tengen to optimize \Ncursed energy would mean
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.47,0:03:05.92,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,only the humans of this nation \Nwould become sorcerers.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.84,0:03:11.33,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,Japan would practically have \Na monopoly on cursed energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.10,0:03:16.00,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,Other nations, especially that superpower, \Nwouldn't stand by and allow that.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.11,0:03:19.76,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,Flesh-and-blood humans \Nwould become an energy source.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.76,0:03:24.01,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,It's easy enough to imagine \Nwhat misfortune that would bring.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.35,0:03:30.52,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,That's a world far removed \Nfrom the ideals I pursue.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.59,0:03:34.14,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,So what?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.83,0:03:37.40,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,For one thing, our objectives are different.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.82,0:03:40.16,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,I don't desire a world \Nwithout cursed spirits
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.38,0:03:43.16,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,or any sort of idyllic peace.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.42,0:03:46.80,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,Non-sorcerers, sorcerers, cursed spirits...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.80,0:03:49.66,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,Those are all possibilities
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.66,0:03:52.54,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,for the shape of cursed \Nenergy that is mankind.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.28,0:03:58.39,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,Though that shouldn't be \Nanywhere near the full extent.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.94,0:04:01.17,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,I tried to give rise
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.17,0:04:03.94,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,to other possibilities \Nfor mankind on my own.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.93,0:04:10.54,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,But that didn't work out.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.54,0:04:12.42,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,Everything that I created myself
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.66,0:04:15.34,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,was limited by the bounds \Nof my own potential.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.78,0:04:21.11,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,The answer was always \Nglimmering darkly within chaos.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.80,0:04:23.20,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,Do you understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.20,0:04:25.30,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,What I should have created
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.30,0:04:28.41,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,was chaos that went \Nbeyond my own control.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.84,0:04:32.41,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,I've already finished \Nextracting the technique.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.55,0:04:36.68,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,There was a cursed spirit \Ncalled Mahito, right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.68,0:04:39.26,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,The one with the technique \Nthat let it interfere with souls!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.26,0:04:41.05,Main,Yuji,0000,0000,0000,,That guy absorbed it earlier.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.05,0:04:42.34,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,Seriously?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.93,0:04:46.85,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,Idle Transfiguration.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.61,0:05:12.71,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,Tengen's barrier? No, this is...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.92,0:05:15.33,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,Remote activation of a cursed technique?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.33,0:05:18.92,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,You have my thanks, Yuji Itadori.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.92,0:05:23.42,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,A cursed spirit's mastery of \Ntheir technique ceases to progress
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.42,0:05:26.80,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,from the moment they're absorbed \Nby Cursed Spirit Manipulation.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.10,0:05:30.30,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,Mahito truly matured \Nthrough his fight with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.86,0:05:35.76,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,To be honest, I wanted to have \NJogo, as well, but no matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.42,0:05:38.14,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,What did you do?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.42,0:05:41.33,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,I remotely activated \NIdle Transfiguration on
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.33,0:05:44.25,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,two types of non-sorcerers \Nthat I marked ahead of time.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.08,0:05:56.96,Sign_Basic,Sign,0000,0000,0000,,{\move(384,220,414,220)\c&H080F0E&\3c&H3C4442&\shad0\fs16}Tsu{\3c&H3B4241&}m{\3c&H4B545A&}iki {\3c&H5E7680&}Fushiguro
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.06,0:06:14.06,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,One type was people whom I had absorb \Ncursed objects like Yuji Itadori did,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.65,0:06:18.54,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,and the other was people like Junpei \NYoshino who have cursed techniques,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.54,0:06:21.56,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,but whose brains were \Nstructured like non-sorcerers.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.56,0:06:25.32,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,Now I've adjusted their brains \Nto match those of sorcerers.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.83,0:06:28.45,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,For the former, I gave them \Nthe strength to be vessels,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.45,0:06:32.58,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,and the latter have obtained the \Nability to activate their techniques.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.88,0:06:35.22,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,And now...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.44,0:06:42.33,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,I've released the seal \Non those cursed objects.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.05,0:06:45.54,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,Some of them have been in a deep sleep
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.54,0:06:48.36,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,after being exposed to my \Ncursed energy when I marked them,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.36,0:06:50.36,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,but they'll soon awaken.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.70,0:06:53.66,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,So, starting now,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.66,0:06:57.80,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,I'll have them kill each other in order to \Ndeepen their understanding of cursed energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.44,0:07:01.63,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,I've carefully hand-picked \Nthese people and cursed objects.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.63,0:07:06.66,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,Think of it as unleashing a \Nthousand malevolent Yuji Itadoris.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.36,0:07:08.95,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,A thousand?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.95,0:07:10.22,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,That's conservative.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.58,0:07:13.21,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,You're also underestimating \Nhuman rationality.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.71,0:07:15.35,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,Do you think people will start
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.35,0:07:17.96,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,killing each other just because \Nthey were granted power?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.34,0:07:20.84,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,There's an order to everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.16,0:07:25.02,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,I certainly didn't cut corners like \Nthat when making my preparations.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.46,0:07:27.88,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,Your questions are starting \Nto become shallow.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.88,0:07:33.44,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,He's pissing me off, \Nso let's all beat him up together!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.44,0:07:35.95,Main,Yuji,0000,0000,0000,,I can't move right now, though...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.10,0:07:44.61,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,What's the matter, Uraume?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.81,0:07:47.86,Italics,Uraume,0000,0000,0000,,I regenerated my body with \Na reverse cursed technique...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.24,0:07:49.26,Italics,Uraume,0000,0000,0000,,This is...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.57,0:07:50.48,Main,Uraume,0000,0000,0000,,Poison?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.24,0:07:54.12,Main,Choso,0000,0000,0000,,My blood got mixed with \Nyours through Piercing Blood.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.12,0:07:55.24,Main,Choso,0000,0000,0000,,Of course it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.80,0:07:58.60,Main,Momo,0000,0000,0000,,Wait, we're not getting cover from Mai-chan.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.60,0:08:01.18,Main,Momo,0000,0000,0000,,They might still have \Nmore allies over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.50,0:08:08.00,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,My ally is protecting Aoi, \Nthe girl with the gun, and that suit.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.00,0:08:09.38,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,They don't belong here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.63,0:08:11.20,Main,Panda,0000,0000,0000,,Can you move?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.20,0:08:12.22,Main,Kamo,0000,0000,0000,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.22,0:08:14.73,Main,Kamo,0000,0000,0000,,I can adjust my body heat.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.73,0:08:15.88,Main,Kamo,0000,0000,0000,,No problems here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.76,0:08:20.14,Main,Kusakabe,0000,0000,0000,,I'm so done.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.54,0:08:22.64,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,We were in the middle of our talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.23,0:08:27.08,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,The cursed objects that I distributed \Nare what's left of the sorcerers
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.08,0:08:30.46,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,I've been secretly making pacts \Nwith for a thousand years.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.46,0:08:34.96,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,Of course, I forged my pacts \Nwith more than just sorcerers,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.17,0:08:41.79,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,though my pacts with those were \Nannulled when I obtained this body.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.48,0:08:44.79,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,You don't mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.12,0:08:49.26,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,This is the world of the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.66,0:09:43.47,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,See you later, Yuji Itadori.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.65,0:09:48.15,Main,Yuji,0000,0000,0000,,Gojo-sensei!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.83,0:09:53.16,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,I have high expectations for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.19,0:09:56.48,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,Are you listening, Sukuna?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.81,0:09:57.98,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,It's starting once again.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.14,0:10:06.12,Main,Geto,0000,0000,0000,,The world of Heian, \Nthe golden age of jujutsu!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.01,0:10:28.66,Italics,Announcer,0000,0000,0000,,The following footage was recorded by \Nour crew, who happened to be on-site
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.66,0:10:33.28,Italics,Announcer,0000,0000,0000,,reporting on a different matter at the \Ntime of the incident in Tokyo the other day.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.28,0:10:35.02,Italics,Announcer,0000,0000,0000,,Please have a look.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.30,0:10:40.64,Italics,Reporter,0000,0000,0000,,{\an8}Uh, it's been about ten minutes \Nsince the blackout, I think?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.64,0:10:44.32,Italics,Reporter,0000,0000,0000,,{\an8}It's been a while, \Nand the blackout continues.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.93,0:10:44.32,Main,OldMan,0000,0000,0000,,Something really crazy is going on.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.32,0:10:45.81,Main,Granny,0000,0000,0000,,Sure it's not fake news?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.32,0:10:49.46,Italics,Reporter,0000,0000,0000,,{\an8}We still cannot contact the station, \Nso the cause remains unknown,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.81,0:10:48.36,Main,Oldman,0000,0000,0000,,All the news is covering this, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.36,0:10:52.52,Main,Granny,0000,0000,0000,,Hmm... Well, I'll be getting home \Nlate today, so have a frozen dinner.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.46,0:10:53.24,Italics,Reporter,0000,0000,0000,,{\an8}and we have practically \Nno idea what's going on.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.52,0:10:54.34,Main,Oldman,0000,0000,0000,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.59,0:10:57.42,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,All 23 wards are nearly wiped out.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.42,0:10:59.29,Main,Official(Female),0000,0000,0000,,The safety of the Prime Minister's office,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.29,0:11:01.54,Main,Official(Female),0000,0000,0000,,including the Chief Cabinet \NSecretary, remains uncertain.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.54,0:11:03.72,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,It's a political void!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.72,0:11:05.97,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,A literal hole!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.28,0:11:08.30,Main,Staff(Male),0000,0000,0000,,No matter how low we estimate it,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.30,0:11:11.32,Main,Staff(Male),0000,0000,0000,,we need to make a plan to evacuate \Nat least five million citizens.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.32,0:11:14.98,Main,Official(Female),0000,0000,0000,,Love hotels, campgrounds, ghost towns...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.98,0:11:19.26,Main,Official(Female),0000,0000,0000,,Use whatever you can, as long as it \Nhas the bare minimum infrastructure.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.26,0:11:22.77,Main,Staff(Female),0000,0000,0000,,More importantly, how are we \Nsupposed to explain this to the residents?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.77,0:11:25.58,Main,Staff(Male),0000,0000,0000,,There's no point announcing anything \Nwhen we don't know the cause!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.37,0:11:30.10,Italics,Reporter,0000,0000,0000,,{\an8}Also, the government has yet \Nto make an announcement.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.37,0:11:32.70,Italics,Reporter,0000,0000,0000,,{\an8}Was this simply the \Nmalfunction of a substation?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.70,0:11:34.16,Italics,Reporter,0000,0000,0000,,{\an8}Was it terrorism?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.37,0:11:38.43,Italics,Reporter,0000,0000,0000,,{\an8}Or perhaps... it was a natural \Ndisaster, like an earthquake?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.04,0:11:39.10,Main,Man,0000,0000,0000,,Too many conspiracy theorists \Nare crawling out.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.76,0:11:40.70,Italics,Reporter,0000,0000,0000,,{\an8}Either way, the cause remains unclear,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.10,0:11:41.63,Main,Woman,0000,0000,0000,,Listen, would you put your phone \Naway and come help me here?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.70,0:11:43.53,Italics,Reporter,0000,0000,0000,,{\an8}and we're being forced to wait \Nwhile they uncover it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.64,0:11:43.53,Main,Man,0000,0000,0000,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:43.98,0:11:46.26,Main,Official(male),0000,0000,0000,,All we can firmly declare \Nsafe are portions of
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.26,0:11:50.15,Main,Official(male),0000,0000,0000,,Okutama, Oume City, Akiruno City, Hachioji City,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.15,0:11:52.22,Main,Official(male),0000,0000,0000,,Machida City, and various islands.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.22,0:11:53.98,Main,Official(male),0000,0000,0000,,For now, you mean.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.98,0:11:57.13,Main,Official(male),0000,0000,0000,,The number of cursed spirits unleashed \Nis no less than ten million.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.13,0:12:00.55,Main,Official(Female),0000,0000,0000,,You want to enact an evacuation order \Non every ward of the entire city?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.55,0:12:02.98,Main,Official(Female),0000,0000,0000,,Afterward, we declare \Nthe wards forbidden to entry.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.98,0:12:04.82,Main,Official(Female),0000,0000,0000,,Make it a real uninhabited zone.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.23,0:12:07.60,Main,Official(Female),0000,0000,0000,,More importantly, \Nwhat about our announcement?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.60,0:12:08.84,Main,Official(Female),0000,0000,0000,,Who's making it?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.84,0:12:11.80,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,Less "who" and more "how" to make it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.80,0:12:13.83,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,We still can't get a hold \Nof the deputy secretary?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.59,0:12:17.42,Main,Official(Female),0000,0000,0000,,No, we can't.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.42,0:12:19.84,Main,Official(Female),0000,0000,0000,,I haven't heard anything \Nfrom his secretary, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.94,0:12:24.25,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,What should we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.25,0:12:27.70,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,Now, now, the upper brass \Nwill figure that out.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.70,0:12:31.53,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,For now, we need to establish \Ncontact with each ministry.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.04,0:12:34.54,Main,Boyfriend,0000,0000,0000,,The low yen ain't stopping.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.54,0:12:36.87,Main,Girlfriend,0000,0000,0000,,That was at least good for exports, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.20,0:12:38.94,Main,Staff(Male),0000,0000,0000,,The Japanese Business \NFederation has lost it?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.94,0:12:41.86,Main,Staff(Female),0000,0000,0000,,They won't be doing any \Nlobbying if everyone's dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.82,0:12:45.36,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,Move the Prime Minister to Osaka!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.36,0:12:48.36,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,At this rate, there'll be a massive \Noutbreak of cursed spirits everywhere!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.71,0:12:52.15,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,Most jujutsu sorcerers are already assigned \Nto protecting evacuees in the city!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.15,0:12:53.54,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,And that outbreak is coming now!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.54,0:12:55.50,Main,Official(Female),0000,0000,0000,,With a power vacuum of this scale,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.50,0:12:57.38,Main,Official(Female),0000,0000,0000,,we may see military intervention \Nfrom other nations.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.38,0:12:59.16,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,Yes. Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.16,0:13:00.38,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,Oh, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.38,0:13:01.26,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.31,0:13:03.38,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.04,0:13:08.45,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,They're going to publicly announce \Nthe existence of cursed spirits.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.45,0:13:09.46,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,Huh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.46,0:13:11.72,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,They're going public with cursed spirits?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.72,0:13:13.06,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,Are they seriously suggesting that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.06,0:13:17.27,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,Apparently, they intend to announce \Nthat cursed spirits only arise in Tokyo.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.27,0:13:20.23,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,So the goal is to direct the populace's \Nleaking cursed energy to Tokyo
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.23,0:13:23.40,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,and limit the outbreak of \Ncursed spirits to there, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.40,0:13:27.82,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,This is why I recommended Itami as a potential \Nrelocation site after Kansai Airport was built!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.82,0:13:30.10,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,Maybe it's better this way?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.10,0:13:33.80,Main,Official(Male),0000,0000,0000,,They wouldn't have reached this decision \Nif Kasumigaseki was functioning.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.58,0:13:39.57,Italics,Reporter,0000,0000,0000,,{\an8}Um, once again, we're sharing the latest.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.57,0:13:42.46,Italics,Reporter,0000,0000,0000,,{\an8}The blackout still continues as before,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.48,0:13:44.33,Italics,Reporter,0000,0000,0000,,{\an8}and we're unable to contact anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.33,0:13:48.61,Italics,Reporter,0000,0000,0000,,{\an8}There's been no official announcement, either, \Nso the cause remains unknown.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.61,0:13:51.84,Italics,Reporter,0000,0000,0000,,{\an8}The question is, how long will this last—hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.61,0:14:04.36,Sign_Basic,Screen,0000,0000,0000,,{\fs18\shad0\c&HCED2D6&\3c&H1B0ABC&\pos(320,288)}LIVE               {\3c&HCED2D6&\c&H393B41&}Unusual Phenomenon in the Capital? Damage Is Spreading
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.98,0:14:00.55,Italics,Cameraman,0000,0000,0000,,{\an8}What?  What is that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.92,0:14:01.94,Italics,Cameraman,0000,0000,0000,,{\an8}Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.11,0:14:08.11,Main,Screen,0000,0000,0000,,{\pos(320,155)\fs20\bord0\shad1\c&HD6DDD5&}Please wait a moment
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.11,0:14:13.83,Sign_Basic,Screen,0000,0000,0000,,{\fs14\bord0\shad0\c&HD6DDD5&\pos(270,123)}Please wait a moment
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.82,0:14:16.31,Main,Woman,0000,0000,0000,,Huh? What is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.61,0:14:17.88,Main,Woman,0000,0000,0000,,A movie?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.52,0:14:25.16,Main,ImperialDirector,0000,0000,0000,,The barrier centered around the Imperial \NPalace that was erected in the Meiji era,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.16,0:14:27.81,Main,ImperialDirector,0000,0000,0000,,and the barrier centered directly \Nabove the Tombs of the Star Corridor,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.81,0:14:30.51,Main,ImperialDirector,0000,0000,0000,,which was a proposed site for the \Nrelocation of Tokyo in the Bakumatsu era,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.51,0:14:33.69,Main,ImperialDirector,0000,0000,0000,,will be forcibly expanded out \Nto the borders of the prefecture.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.29,0:15:43.91,Main,Woman,0000,0000,0000,,Come.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.91,0:15:45.65,Main,Woman,0000,0000,0000,,Come.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.65,0:15:47.76,Main,Woman,0000,0000,0000,,It's dangerous here.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.30,0:16:00.15,Main,Woman,0000,0000,0000,,I have a warm bath.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.01,0:16:07.58,Main,Woman,0000,0000,0000,,I can sing songs, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.53,0:16:15.40,Main,Girl,0000,0000,0000,,What about my mom?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.80,0:16:20.42,Main,Woman,0000,0000,0000,,Your mother, father,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.42,0:16:24.83,Main,Woman,0000,0000,0000,,older sister, younger brother,\Nand teacher are all here.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.51,0:16:30.07,Main,Girl,0000,0000,0000,,I don't have a younger brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.07,0:16:32.05,Main,Girl,0000,0000,0000,,And I hate my teacher.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.05,0:16:35.99,Main,Woman,0000,0000,0000,,I don't have a younger brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.99,0:16:40.47,Main,Woman,0000,0000,0000,,And I hate my teacher.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.56,0:16:43.20,Main,Girl,0000,0000,0000,,Are you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.20,0:16:44.45,Main,Girl,0000,0000,0000,,Need a drink?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.56,0:16:52.12,Main,Woman,0000,0000,0000,,Please?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.98,0:17:28.07,Main,Okkotsu,0000,0000,0000,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.64,0:17:31.16,Main,Okkotsu,0000,0000,0000,,Did I scare you?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.87,0:17:35.07,Main,Okkotsu,0000,0000,0000,,Are you hurt?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.96,0:17:40.02,Main,Okkotsu,0000,0000,0000,,Were you with anyone?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.24,0:17:43.72,Main,Okkotsu,0000,0000,0000,,Like your mom or dad?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.08,0:17:46.36,Main,Girl,0000,0000,0000,,I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.54,0:17:49.78,Italics,Okkotsu,0000,0000,0000,,It's all commercial buildings here,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.78,0:17:51.67,Italics,Okkotsu,0000,0000,0000,,so I guess she's not from around here?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.20,0:17:54.86,Main,Okkotsu,0000,0000,0000,,Did you walk a lot?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.22,0:18:01.11,Main,Okkotsu,0000,0000,0000,,I see. You worked hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.72,0:18:10.86,Main,Okkotsu,0000,0000,0000,,You can see them, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.80,0:18:14.22,Main,Okkotsu,0000,0000,0000,,That's bad, Rika-chan.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.14,0:18:16.36,Main,Okkotsu,0000,0000,0000,,Don't overdo it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.83,0:18:21.10,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,I'm sorry. I hesitated.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.71,0:18:24.60,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,I thought I should sit back and watch,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.60,0:18:27.75,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,and give him room to work, since the \Nsituation had already progressed so far.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.04,0:18:30.42,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,Have you realized yet?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.42,0:18:33.56,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,I'm not really on your side.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.28,0:18:39.32,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,I'm just a humble beauty who wants to \Neradicate cursed spirits from the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.61,0:18:42.87,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,It might not be much of an apology,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.87,0:18:48.48,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,but my allies and I will take responsibility \Nfor delivering the kids who were there.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.22,0:18:54.77,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,It's high time I confronted Tengen, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.76,0:19:00.32,Main,Tsukumo,0000,0000,0000,,What will you do?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.46,0:19:09.45,Main,Leader,0000,0000,0000,,Good work, Okkotsu.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.45,0:19:11.64,Main,Okkotsu,0000,0000,0000,,You don't really intend to thank me,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.64,0:19:13.56,Main,Okkotsu,0000,0000,0000,,so let's just get to the point.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.01,0:19:19.22,Main,Okkotsu,0000,0000,0000,,Now you understand that \NI'll obey your orders, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.95,0:19:25.52,Main,Leader,0000,0000,0000,,No amount of killing cursed \Nspirits will prove anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.63,0:19:29.62,Main,Okkotsu,0000,0000,0000,,Then forge a pact or whatever you need to.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.22,0:19:33.02,Main,Okkotsu,0000,0000,0000,,It doesn't matter that he's \None of Gojo-sensei's students.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.36,0:19:38.67,Main,Okkotsu,0000,0000,0000,,He cut off Inumaki-kun's arms in Shibuya.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.12,0:19:44.36,Main,Okkotsu,0000,0000,0000,,So I will kill Yuji Itadori.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.41,0:19:49.91,Sign_Basic,Screen,0000,0000,0000,,{\pos(320,210)\an8\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\shad0}Notice from Jujutsu Headquarters
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.91,0:19:57.92,Sign_Basic,Screen,0000,0000,0000,,{\pos(320,230)\an8\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\shad0}1) Suguru Geto's survival was confirmed.\NWe hereby declare the reinstatement\Nof his death sentence.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.92,0:20:08.43,Sign_Basic,Screen,0000,0000,0000,,{\pos(320,256)\an8\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\shad0}2) Satoru Gojo has been deemed an accomplice in the\NShibuya Incident and is hereby expelled from jujutsu society.\NIn addition, any attempt to free him from his seal will be deemed a crime.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.43,0:20:17.94,Sign_Basic,Screen,0000,0000,0000,,{\pos(320,280)\an8\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\shad0}3) Masamichi Yaga is sentenced to death\Nfor inciting Satoru Gojo and Suguru Geto,\Ncausing the Shibuya Incident.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.94,0:20:25.45,Sign_Basic,Screen,0000,0000,0000,,{\pos(320,230)\an8\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\shad0}4) The suspension on Yuji Itadori's\Ndeath sentence is hereby revoked, and his\Nexecution shall be carried out promptly.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.45,0:20:32.96,Sign_Basic,Screen,0000,0000,0000,,{\pos(320,230)\an8\fnTimes New Roman\bord0\shad0}5) Special-grade sorcerer Yuta Okkotsu\Nshall be appointed as Yuji Itadori's executioner.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.01,0:22:09.78,Ep_Title,Screen,0000,0000,0000,,Episode 47\N{\fs30\fscy150}Shibuya Incident - Gate, Close
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.78,0:22:10.03,Ep_Title,Screen,0000,0000,0000,,{\fnTimes New Roman\fs18\b1\an3\bord0\shad0\c&HEEF7FA&\pos(553,330)}To Be Continued

